From f8dbd39ade99c0fdc45df07a238204bd96da7e5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: postmarketos-note8 <noreply@postmarketos-note8>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:52:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: new 'shannon' plugin for the Samsung Shannon CP of
 Exynos SoCs

The integrated Shannon CP of Exynos SoCs (e.g. Exynos 8895, Galaxy Note 8)
on a mainline kernel with the modem_v1 driver (mif_sipc5): one AT port on
the WWAN subsystem and raw-IP rmnet net ports. A PDP context reaches rmnet
only when it is set up over Samsung IPC; the userspace helper that owns
IPC serves the AT port and implements AT+CGACT=1/0, AT+CGACT? and
AT+CGCONTRDP for that call. The bearer activates with +CGACT, configures
the net port statically from +CGCONTRDP and never uses PPP.
---
